    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i'm hitting an \"Access Denied\" error with an S3 bucket. im trying to let a lambda function write logs to it but the policy doesnt seem to be working. can you look at this json and tell me what im doing wrong?\n\n{\n  \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n  \"Statement\": [\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Action\": [\n        \"s3:PutObject\"\n      ],\n      \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:s3:::my-log-bucket\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The issue is that your resource ARN is missing the object path component. For permissions to work on objects *within* the bucket, you must specify everyone that includes `/*`. Correct your `Resource` to `\"arn:aws:s3:::my-log-bucket/*\"`. Also, ensure your Lambda execution role explicitly trusts an AWS service principal, which is a separate configuration from this bucket policy.",
      "source": "target",
