    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "ohhh okay that makes sense. i didnt realize i had to include the /* at the end of the bucket name. i'll try adding that now. \n\none more thing though - i also have a bucket policy on the bucket itself, not just the iam role. should i be adding the same thing there or is that redundant? im just worried about making it too open since these are sensitive logs.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Both the IAM role policy attached to your Lambda and the S3 bucket policy need to allow the action, but they serve different purposes. If the Lambda's role policy allows access, it is generally sufficient unless you need an explicit cross-account access grant. To keep it secure, ensure the bucket policy *only* grants permission to your specific Lambda's IAM Role ARN, rather than using a broad principal like \"AWS.\"",
      "source": "target",
