      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks, that clears things up. i'll tighten up the principal to just the role arn then. \n\nactually i just realized i saw some weird logs in CloudTrail earlier about 'unauthorized attempts' even before i started messing with this. it's kinda stressing me out that someone might be trying to poke around in our logs. how do i actually check if someone (or some service) is actively trying to bypass these permissions?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The best way to check for active permission bypass attempts is to closely monitor your CloudTrail logs specifically for `AccessDenied` errors in the context of S3 API calls. You can create a CloudWatch Metric Filter or use Athena to query CloudTrail events, filtering on the status code for authorization failures. Reviewing the principal (identity) associated with these denied actions will show you *who* is attempting the suspicious access.",
      "source": "target",
